# Wear all four Rings of Elemental Command, two at a time, and let wizard
# mode print the magnitude of the command ability each one grants. Read by
# tools/check_ring_command_level.sh, finding PA-08-F4 of bd inc-tek.8.8.
#
# WHY THIS ORACLE. The number a ring grants is an effective priest turning
# level, which src/Skills.cpp:4448-4562 adds to a d20 roll and to several
# other bonuses before it divides by the target's resistance. Two extra points
# move a probability and cross no visible threshold, so no amount of watching
# the game command creatures would measure it. Wizard mode's "Examine Player
# Data" prints every stati with its Val and its Mag (src/Debug.cpp:1528-1584),
# and that Mag IS the number this finding changes. Val names the element:
# MA_WATER 92, MA_AIR 93, MA_EARTH 94, MA_FIRE 95 (inc/Defines.h:1610-1613).
#
# The character sheet cannot do this job. Its CA_COMMAND case
# (src/Sheet.cpp:492-499) prints the element and no number at all, unlike the
# CA_TURNING case beside it.
#
# WHY TWO PASSES. A creature has two ring slots, so only two of the four rings
# can be worn at once. The script wears Water and Fire, dumps the stati, then
# swaps Air and Earth in over the top and dumps again. All four rings are
# therefore measured in one session.
#
#   w y                      enter wizard mode and open its menu. The second
#                            and later 'w' need no 'y': the confirmation is
#                            asked once, when WizardMode goes true
#                            (src/Player.cpp:773-784).
#   Item Acquisition         RIGHT*26 walks the glyph row to Rings: ItemGlyphs
#   RIGHT*26                 (src/Tables.cpp:320) puts -AI_RING 26 steps along.
#   @until "<name>" DOWN     the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#                            cursor is walked. Three rows show and the MIDDLE
#                            one is selected, so the run stops on the pass
#                            where the row BELOW the wanted one appears. The
#                            four rings sit in file order in lib/m_items.irh
#                            (Air, Earth, Fire, Water) and Item Preservation
#                            follows Water. The check does not trust that
#                            ordering: it reads every ring's name back off the
#                            inventory screen before it believes any number.
#   ENTER m|n SPACE          take it, move the cursor to a ring slot -- 'm' is
#                            Left Ring and 'n' is Right Ring -- and SPACE to
#                            put it on (src/Managers.cpp:873).
#   s                        stow whatever the swap left in the air. A ring put
#                            on over an occupied slot pushes the old ring into
#                            the in-air slot, and the manager refuses to close
#                            while anything is held there. 's' puts it in the
#                            pack (src/Managers.cpp:835-848), which also takes
#                            its command ability away again.
#   ESC w                    leave the manager and reopen the wizard menu.
#   @until "COMMAND ABILITY" the debug dump is far longer than one screen and
#     DOWN                   scrolls with DOWN, not PGDN (src/Debug.cpp:583-596).
#   DOWN*6                   the first COMMAND ABILITY arrives on the bottom
#                            row. Six more rows bring the second one, and the
#                            ring name printed under each, into view.

@include chargen.keys

# --- pass one: Water on the left hand, Fire on the right ---
w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*26
@until "Ring of Item Preservation" DOWN
ENTER
m
SPACE
ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*26
@until "Ring of Elemental Command (Water)" DOWN
ENTER
n
SPACE
@dump:rings-on
ESC
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
@until "COMMAND ABILITY" DOWN
DOWN*6
@dump:stati
ESC

# --- pass two: Air replaces Water, Earth replaces Fire ---
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*26
@until "Ring of Elemental Command (Earth)" DOWN
ENTER
m
SPACE
s
ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*26
@until "Ring of Elemental Command (Fire)" DOWN
ENTER
n
SPACE
s
@dump:rings-on2
ESC
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
@until "COMMAND ABILITY" DOWN
DOWN*6
@dump:stati2
